From 9c2ac4f3094260e028c46aa1f06b2ccc5533868c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: testuser <mainta@example.test>
Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 17:50:37 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 15/15] fix(core): raise the default command limit to 10
 minutes

- Give run_commands, the model command tool, a 600000 ms default.
  Keep source changes and tests together in fork patch 0015.
- Let CLINE_RUN_COMMANDS_TIMEOUT_MS set the command limit in milliseconds.
  Accept plain digits from 1000 ms through 1800000 ms.
  Cap larger values, including digit strings too long for a number.
  Use the default for other values.
  No setting removes the limit.
- Share one resolved limit between the tool and shell executor.
  Keep host settings in code ahead of the environment variable.
  Keep stand-alone defaults at 30000 ms for other callers.
- State the limit: "Each command is stopped after 600 seconds."
  Tell the model to keep suitable builds, installs and tests foreground.
  Keep servers, watchers and longer work in background.
- Send rejected-setting and capped-setting warnings to stderr.
  Print each distinct warning once.
  Clear timeout timers when commands finish.
  Keep other tools' limits at 30000 ms.
- Before the change, 3 test files could not load.
  Another 2 tests failed.
  A stub keeping 30000 ms failed 33 of 41 tests.
- All 41 new tests pass after the change.
  shell-timeout.test.ts has 11 tests.
  builtin-shell-timeout.test.ts has 21 tests.
  builtin-shell-executor-timeout.test.ts has 6 tests.
  with-timeout.test.ts has 3 tests.
- Leave the linux-arm64 build and promotion for later.
  Run the fork gate when the binary is built.
- Resolve once in createBuiltinTools. The 1000 ms floor, the stderr warning, exact seconds in the description and its wording follow from that.
- This patch moves the worker image key and joins the next promotion.
